CM Example 1 :	Dipole in free space 	
CM See GetStarted.txt
CM 
CM 
CM 
CM 
CM forw: 90, 0 ; back: 90, 180
CE
SY LA=0.0541632	'length
SY R= 1e-3	'Radius of the wavelength
SY LR=0.0597	'Length of the lefthand wire
SY lambda=0.125
SY LD = 0.0488	'Length of the righthand wires
SY deltaR =0.02708	'Distance to the lefthand wire
SY deltaD =0.02708	'Increment of distance of the righthand wires
GW	1	11	0	0	LA/2	0	0	-LA/2	R	'Wire 1, 11 segments, halve wavelength long.
GW	2	11	-deltaR	0	LR/2	-deltaR	0	-LR/2	R
GW	3	11	deltaD	0	LD/2	deltaD	0	-LD/2	R
GW	4	11	deltaD*2	0	LD/2	deltaD*2	0	-LD/2	R
GW	5	11	deltaD*3	0	LD/2	deltaD*3	0	-LD/2	R
GE	0
GN	-1
EK
EX	0	1	6	0	1	0	0	'Voltage source (1+j0) at wire 1 segment 5.
FR,0,1,0,0,2400
PQ -1
PT -1
RP,0,37,73,1003,-180,0,5,5
